module

public import Theory.Representation.SL5ExteriorSquare.DecomposablePreserver.NormalizerAction

/-!
# Decomposable preservers of the binary exterior square

Every linear equivalence of Λ²(F₂⁵) that preserves the nonzero decomposable
orbit is the exterior square of an element of SL₅(2). The exported normalizer
application realizes the actual conjugation transported by a given marking.
The proof classifies totally decomposable four-spaces as stars, using the
Grassmann clique theorem of Meierfrankenfeld–Stellmacher (1993), (1.6),
pp.845–847, and reconstructs the natural matrix from five standard stars.
-/
